### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- description: English-first US equity value-investing skill with bilingual (EN/中文) guidance. Use when you need to evaluate US stocks with a structured value framework: quality + moat + management + valuation + risk controls, generate buy/hold/avoid recommendations, run scenario/reverse-DCF style checks, and set daily/weekly monitoring rules for portfolio decisions.
- # US Value Investing Framework (EN + 中文)
- A practical, reusable framework for analyzing US stocks in the spirit of the X article’s “value investing skill,” expanded into a full decision system.
- ## Quick workflow
- 1. Define thesis and time horizon.
- 2. Collect core inputs (fundamentals, business quality, risk flags).
- 3. Score company quality + valuation.
- 4. Classify into **Buy / Watch / Avoid**.
- 5. Set monitoring thresholds and rebalance rules.
- ## Core outputs
- - Investment memo (English-first, with Chinese summary)
- - Numeric scorecard (0–100)
- - Risk flags list
- - Suggested action: `buy`, `watch`, `avoid`
- - Monitoring checklist for daily/weekly review
- ## Run the bundled evaluator
- Prepare an input JSON (see `references/input-template.json`), then run:
-   --out .state/aapl-eval.json \
-   --markdown .state/aapl-eval.md
- ## Scoring model (expanded)
- The evaluator computes a weighted score:
- - **Quality (30%)**: ROIC, gross margin, FCF margin, debt discipline
- - **Growth durability (20%)**: revenue growth, FCF growth, stability
- - **Moat & governance (15%)**: moat strength, management quality, capital allocation
- - **Valuation (25%)**: P/E, EV/EBIT, FCF yield, optional intrinsic-value gap
- - **Risk penalty (10%)**: concentration, leverage shock, policy/regulatory risk, accounting flags
- Final output includes:
- - `total_score`
- - `verdict`: buy/watch/avoid
- - `confidence`: high/medium/low
- ## Suggested thresholds (default)
- - `>= 75`: Buy candidate (with sizing discipline)
- - `60–74`: Watch / wait for better price
- - `< 60`: Avoid or keep on low-priority list
- ## Monitoring rules (for automation/cron)
- Daily:
- - Price drawdown from thesis entry
- - Valuation percentile change
- - News/event risk tags
- Weekly:
- - Guidance revisions
- - Earnings estimate drift
- - Balance-sheet stress checks
- Quarterly:
- - Earnings call thesis check
- - Capital allocation behavior review
- - Scorecard refresh
- ## Bilingual report guidance
- Default writing style:
- - Main body in English
- - Add a concise Chinese section: “中文结论（摘要）”
- - Keep numbers identical across EN/CN
- ## Resource map
- - `scripts/evaluate_company.py`: deterministic score engine
- - `references/framework-guide.md`: extended methodology and writing pattern
+ description: US stock valuation model skill (English-first + 中文) based on financial report data. Use when you need to apply explicit rules: ROE > 15% for 3+ years, debt ratio < 50%, free cash flow > 80% of net income, moat assessment (brand/network effect/cost advantage), then output investment rating (A/B/C/D) with reasons.
+ # US Stock Valuation Model - Value Investing Framework (EN + 中文)
+ This skill is an explicit rule-based value model focused on US stocks.
+ ## Input
+ Company financial report data (structured JSON), including:
+ - 3+ years of ROE
+ - Debt ratio
+ - Free cash flow and net income
+ - Moat assessment: brand / network effect / cost advantage
+ Use the bundled template: `references/input-template.json`.
+ ## Decision Rules (strict)
+ 1. **ROE rule**: ROE > 15% for at least 3 consecutive years
+ 2. **Leverage rule**: Debt ratio < 50%
+ 3. **Cash conversion rule**: Free cash flow > 80% of net income
+ 4. **Moat rule**: evaluate brand/network effect/cost advantage
+ ## Output
+ - Investment rating: **A / B / C / D**
+ - Reasons (pass/fail explanation per rule)
+ - Bilingual summary (EN main + 中文摘要)
+ ## Run
+   --out .state/eval.json \
+   --markdown .state/eval.md
+ ## Rating policy
+ - **A**: all 4 rules pass
+ - **B**: 3 rules pass
+ - **C**: 2 rules pass
+ - **D**: 0-1 rule pass
+ ## Resources
+ - `scripts/evaluate_company.py`: deterministic evaluator

